ant in the context of predicting vehicle type.\ndf.drop(columns=['HOLLOWS_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS is dropped\n# The SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS feature has a low mean (Mean = 6.3176) and small standard deviation (Std = 4.9595), indicating limited variability. Its range and influence on vehicle classification are likely small, and it may not provide informative differentiation compared to other features.\ndf.drop(columns=['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column CIRCULARITY is dropped\n# The CIRCULARITY feature is highly correlated with COMPACTNESS (both are computed using area and radius), and thus may be redundant. To reduce multicollinearity and simplify the feature space, it is beneficial to remove this feature.\ndf.drop(columns=['CIRCULARITY'], inplace=True)\n```end", "```python\n# Feature name: COMPACTNESS_SQRT\n# Feature description: Square root of COMPACTNESS\n# Usefulness: Reduces the scale of the values in COMPACTNESS, potentially capturing non-linear relationships. This transformation may reveal hidden patterns in classification tasks, particularly when dealing with potentially non-linear decision boundaries in the feature space.\n\ndf['COMPACTNESS_SQRT'] = np.sqrt(df['COMPACTNESS'])\n```end\n\n```python\n# Feature name: SCATTER_RATIO_ELONGATEDNESS_RATIO\n# Feature description: Ratio of SCATTER_RATIO to ELONGATEDNESS\n# Usefulness: Combines two features related to the shape and distribution of the silhouette to form a new ratio feature. This could capture interactions between the compactness of the shape and how elongated it is (e.g., identifying unique shapes of specific vehicle types).\n\ndf['SCATTER_RATIO_ELONGATEDNESS_RATIO'] = df['SCATTER_RATIO'] / df['ELONGATEDNESS']\n```end\n\n```python\n# Feature name: SCALED_RADIUS_CIRCULARITY_COMBO\n# Feature description: The product of SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION and CIRCULARITY\n# Usefulness: Combines the circular distribution of the silhouette (CIRCULARITY) with the overall distribution of mass (SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION). This may help in identifying specific types of vehicles with consistent relationships between compactness and spread.\n\ndf['SCALED_RADIUS_CIRCULARITY_COMBO'] = df['SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION'] * df['CIRCULARITY']\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS is dropped\n# The values of SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS have a very narrow range (0–22) and are highly skewed, with Q1 and Q3 indicating a large proportion of the data is clustered at the lower end (Q1 = 2, Median = 5, Q3 = 9). This feature likely offers low variance and discriminatory power for classification tasks.\n\ndf.drop(columns=['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column HOLLOWS_RATIO is dropped\n# HOLLOWS_RATIO has an extremely small range (181–211) and low standard deviation, suggesting limited variability. This makes it unlikely to contribute significant value to separating the four vehicle classes.\n\ndf.drop(columns=['HOLLOWS_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO is dropped\n# MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO has a narrow range (3–52), with most of the data clustered between 7 and 10. Given the dataset already has features like PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO and SCATTER_RATIO, which may provide similar or complementary information about shape proportions, it is unnecessary to retain this column.\n\ndf.drop(columns=['MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n### Reasoning for Feature Engineering Steps:\n\n1. **Square Root of COMPACTNESS (`COMPACTNESS_SQRT`)**: \n    - Many machine learning algorithms, especially tree-based methods and linear models, can perform better when input features are distributed in a less skewed, more normalized manner. Taking a square root can help stabilize variance and ensure that larger values do not disproportionately affect the model.\n\n2. **Ratio of SCATTER_RATIO and ELONGATEDNESS (`SCATTER_RATIO_ELONGATEDNESS_RATIO`)**:\n    - Ratios often provide information about how two quantities interact, forming more interpretable features. By creating a new feature that links `SCATTER_RATIO` and `ELONGATEDNESS`, we can enhance our model’s ability to distinguish different vehicle classes by capturing unique relationships between the compactness of the scatter and the elongated shape.\n\n3. **Combination of SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION and CIRCULARITY (`SCALED_RADIUS_CIRCULARITY_COMBO`)**:\n    - CIRCULARITY reflects how round the vehicle is, while SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION captures the distribution of mass relative to the area. By multiplying these two, we are likely to capture a new composite property of the silhouette's geometry that could help the model differentiate more nuanced features associated with specific vehicle types.\n\n### Justifications for Dropping Certain Features:\n- Each dropped feature was evaluated for low variance, high correlation with other features, or limited discriminatory power, which could introduce noise into the model rather than aid prediction tasks."]
