python
# Feature name: LOG_COMPACTNESS
# Feature description: Logarithm of compactness (log(COMPACTNESS)).
# Usefulness: Compactness represents how tightly the area is packed within its perimeter, which plays a key role in classifying vehicle shapes viewed from different angles. Taking a logarithmic transformation can reduce skewness in the feature distribution and help algorithms better differentiate between subtle variations in compactness across vehicle types.
df['LOG_COMPACTNESS'] = np.log(df['COMPACTNESS'])
end

---

python
# Feature name: RADIUS_VARIANCE
# Feature description: Difference between scaled variance along the minor axis and scaled variance along the major axis (SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS - SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MAJOR_AXIS).
# Usefulness: This feature measures the imbalance in the spread of the object along its two axes. A significant variance difference could indicate the unique silhouette characteristics of certain vehicle types, such as the narrow body of a VAN or the wide body of a BUS.
df['RADIUS_VARIANCE'] = df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS'] - df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MAJOR_AXIS']
end

---

python
# Feature name: NORMALIZED_HOLLOWS_RATIO
# Feature description: The hollows ratio normalized by the PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY (HOLLOWS_RATIO / PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY).
# Usefulness: A normalized hollows ratio could capture the extent of hollow regions in the vehicle's silhouette adjusted for its overall shape and bounding. This can help differentiate vehicles like a VAN, which might have a hollow shape related to its function as a transport vehicle.
df['NORMALIZED_HOLLOWS_RATIO'] = df['HOLLOWS_RATIO'] / df['PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY']
end

